                                        "entry_id": "7ff61fef-25df-33eb-9682-9cede03a8b4d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Small, smooth pebbles, as found on a beach."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8f1a93a4-5ea7-40d6-a3a9-f5c33b9bf0a3",
                                                "sense_id": "95c5ee7c-d6c3-34fc-8928-cf2e5c28ea72",
                                                "text": "And naked shingles of the world."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cdcbf763-73ec-4f1c-a96f-e1f169e5ff7e",
                                                "sense_id": "95c5ee7c-d6c3-34fc-8928-cf2e5c28ea72",
                                                "text": "Underneath a black cliff where the incoming tide smashed on the shingle, they stumbled upon the mail hood of Hrothgar's murdered vassal."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0ffeb6ab-d339-40c1-8210-66b479c09e31",
                                                "sense_id": "95c5ee7c-d6c3-34fc-8928-cf2e5c28ea72",
                                                "text": "You need to excavate and remove the topsoil, line the subsoil with a geotextile, then lay and compact hardcore. Follow this with a layer of compacted \"hoggin\" – compacted clay, gravel and sand. This is then sprayed with hot bitumen, and has a layer of pea shingle rolled into it."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f4951a84-0a31-4ade-a6ff-d84f9a56bfb0",
                                                "sense_id": "95c5ee7c-d6c3-34fc-8928-cf2e5c28ea72",
                                                "text": "One can't escape the huge nuclear facility at Sellafield (supplier of much of the line's remaining freight traffic), or miss the wild shingle beaches with exposed and precarious bungalows sandwiched between the railway and the shore at Braystones."
                                            }
